6198490 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1045 "Computing Triple Integrals Using a Change of Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186199269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1050 1080.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198490 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9c0cd1dd-d41d-511e-aa18-44cf1df53bbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199269 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199269 #edb/ref 1061 42964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199269 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c8fb7bf0-e270-5a21-96df-05f4bb90a104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199269 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199311 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199311 #edb/ref 1061 44576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199311 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9ff6a5f7-0ed3-5407-9add-6b4b8b9f9576" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199311 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199312 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199312 #edb/ref 1061 44578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199312 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "72db4d82-680c-5663-9ec8-49034717bf11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199312 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199313 #edb/ref 1061 44583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199313 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "63e21bf5-1c47-551b-9e3f-4385831c5ab7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199313 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199461 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that the transformation $\\mathbf T,$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T: (u,v,w) \\longrightarrow \\left(x(u,v,w), \\, y(u,v,w), \\, z(u,v,w) \\right)\n$$\n\nis a $C^1$ transformation that has no critical points (i.e., it is invertible) inside some region $\\Delta\\subset \\mathbb R^3,$ and that $\\mathbf T(\\Delta) = R,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/d7/d7875753545cba8babd08fccaf55236c6b32bfc56f43f496343174acc198f1d9.png)\n\n \n\nTo compute the integral of a function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R,$ we use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\iiint\\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\ \\mathrm{d}V = \\iiint\\limits_{\\Delta} \\ f(x(u,v,w), y(u,v,w), z(u,v,w)) \\: \\left| \\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)} \\right|  \\: \\textrm{d}u \\textrm{d}v \\textrm{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $\\mathbf{T}.$\n\nNote the similarity with the change of variables formula for double integrals." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199461 #edb/ref 1065 7217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199461 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a43397ab-8a32-5928-ba64-90ad84532ab1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199461 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374083 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374083 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374083 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374083 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x+y\\le 2,\\,0\\le y-x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+y,\\,v=y-x,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2(x+y){e}^{y-x}\\,dV={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374083 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2efc4cf1-75d6-520b-94c1-d854f8fd8b64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374083 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+y,\\,v=y-x,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v,w)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1,\\,0\\le w\\le 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(1+1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2(x+y){e}^{y-x}\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}2u{e}^{v}\\cdot |\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}2u{e}^{v}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,u{e}^{v}\\,\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186374086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374084 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9448f758-7aaf-5272-b5f6-88f1b32ee8d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374085 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{u}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374085 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374085 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "19590723-9dbc-594f-9f4e-6ca0160553fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374086 #edb/ref 1080 "u{e}^{v}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374086 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374086 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e319ca87-b89a-5147-977c-a329bf0ff49e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374087 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{v{e}^{u}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374087 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374087 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e89988d6-d0a3-55a0-b505-58a6138e15f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374088 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{v}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374088 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374088 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "26fa2b15-0257-541e-aadc-bc6d9526fdc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374089 #edb/ref 1080 "2u{e}^{v}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374089 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186374089 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fbfe48d4-fab5-5337-a025-f32c4db8dd7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401302 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401302 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161879" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401302 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401302 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x+3y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le z-3y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+3y,\\,v=z-3y,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{cos}^{2}⁡(x+z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(z-3y)\\,dV={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401302 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4004275e-59e4-54d2-bbaa-29203ac29308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401302 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+3y,\\,v=z-3y,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le w\\le 2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-3-0) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{cos}^{2}⁡(x+z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(z-3y)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}{cos}^{2}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot |\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{cos}^{2}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{3}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\frac{1}{3}{cos}^{2}⁡(u+v)\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186401303 #edb/ref 1075 #e