edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b31ba118-b4ec-54ec-bb50-628c0cc67dda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522438 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522438 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522438 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c921974f-fc45-5558-acc3-f2310130ec21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522524 #edb/ref 1080 "\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522524 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522524 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ec8b09ec-156b-5830-8ce7-eac0fbd892c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522542 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{v}\\frac{u\\operatorname{sinh}⁡u}{2}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522542 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522542 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f6cc9b29-5be4-54fe-8424-7c6e39a3e9a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186522161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522591 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4072ebe9-e356-5a8b-bdd6-bdedd4bc5d7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186522330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522666 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e00110c2-7288-57e8-9508-75b52e302e96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186522386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186522323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522688 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fd889248-045c-5336-9e14-01871b41eb76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522753 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522753 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39062" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522753 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522753 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{x}\\le y\\le \\frac{2}{x},\\,\\frac{1}{xy}\\le z\\le \\frac{2}{xy}\\}.\n$$\n\nBy performing the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x,\\,v=xy,\\,w=xyz,\n$$\n\nthe triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\,{e}^{xyz}\\,dV\n$$\n\ncan be written in terms of $u,$ $v,$ and $w$ as" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522753 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a7a1582-d778-5af4-af63-1b6090d14c6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522753 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$ \n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x,\\,v=xy,\\,w=xyz\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,1\\le v\\le 2,\\,1\\le w\\le 2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ y & x & 0 \\\\ yz & xz & xy\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =xy|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ y & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =xy(x-0) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y \\\\  & =uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{uv}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{e}^{xyz}\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}{e}^{w}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{uv}|\\,\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{{e}^{w}}{uv}\\,\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{{e}^{w}}{uv}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522780 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522780 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162128" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522780 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522780 #edb/ref 1071 "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=2x+y,\\,v=3x+2z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{12}{1+(3x+2z)^{2}}\\,dV,\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\le 2x+y\\le \\frac{2}{\\pi },\\,\\,0\\le 3x+2z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522780 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c40cfd48-e992-514e-93b1-f5d1aa09838d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522780 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=2x+y,\\,v=3x+2z,\\,w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\le u\\le \\frac{2}{\\pi },\\,0\\le v\\le 1,\\,0\\le w\\le 2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{12}{1+(3x+2z)^{2}}\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{12}{1+{v}^{2}}\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{3}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{4}{(1+{v}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/\\pi }^{2/\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4}{(1+{v}^{2})}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/\\pi }^{2/\\pi }\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4}{(1+{v}^{2})}\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}dw \\\\  & =[u]_{1/\\pi }^{2/\\pi }\\cdot {[4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡v]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{\\pi })\\cdot (4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}-0)\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522809 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186522591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522809 #edb/ref 1069 "q-39056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522809 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522809 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\le 2,\\,2\\le x+y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nBy performing the change of variables\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,v=x+y,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\nthe triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x+y)\\operatorname{sinh}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,dV\n$$\n\ncan be written in terms of $u,$ $v,$ and $w$ as" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522809 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f849acac-b165-56ce-af0c-ee1d4893cc84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522809 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$ \n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,v=x+y,\\,w=z,\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps: \n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & =\\{(u,v,w)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,2\\le v\\le 4,\\,0\\le w\\le 1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & -2y & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2x & -2y \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2x+2y \\\\  & =2(x+y) \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$ \n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+y)\\operatorname{sinh}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}v\\operatorname{sinh}⁡u\\cdot |\\frac{1}{2v}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡u}{2}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡u}{2}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522824 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522824 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1da0db94-3628-5190-a1fe-f76eb1f4550b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522824 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186374083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522843 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522843 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5e5891c8-8277-54c3-9c11-9481ab910bf8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522843 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186522809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522862 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186522824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522862 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9415b5d7-f308-5c17-9e90-f8ba5c185823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522862 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186401302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186522865 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 175921865228